@startuml fig1_control_kinds
' Diagram 1 of the IEC 60050-351 pattern: kind of control, action path, action.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - the action line and what it runs between, the forward and feedback paths
'    of a control loop, and the units of Figures 1 and 2: diagram 2
'  - functions and characteristics: diagram 3
'  - OptimalControl, ProgrammedControl and ComputerControl, which sit directly
'    under Control because 351-47-20 and 351-47-52 name no genus, and the eight
'    kinds below ClosedLoopControl: diagram 5 carries the full hierarchy
'
' No class for automating stands between Control and the two kinds of control.
' The standard defines automating in 351-43 as a task, not in 351-47 as a kind
' of control, and a hand-operated closed-loop control is one without being
' automated. That notion belongs to the AI pattern and to the alignment.
'
' Read top to bottom: the kind of control, then the two conditions that decide
' it, then what carries it out. Structure and behaviour are two columns, since
' the point of the pattern is that they are two conditions and not one.
'
' The four relations start at Control, not at Automation, because that is their
' domain in the ontology. Automation inherits them. Drawing them at Automation
' would claim a restriction the model does not make.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

class Control
class OpenLoopControl
class ClosedLoopControl

class Action
class OpenAction
class ClosedAction

class ActionPath
class OpenActionPath
class ClosedActionPath

class ControlChain
class ControlLoop

' --- the kind of control -------------------------------------------
Control <|-- OpenLoopControl
Control <|-- ClosedLoopControl

' --- the two conditions ---------------------------------------------
Action <|-- OpenAction
Action <|-- ClosedAction

ActionPath <|-- OpenActionPath
ActionPath <|-- ClosedActionPath

' --- what carries out the automation --------------------------------
' --- relations -------------------------------------------------------
Control --> "1" Action      : hasAction
Control --> "1" ActionPath  : runsOverActionPath
Action     -down-> "1" ActionPath  : actionOverPath
Control --> ControlChain    : realisedBy
Control --> ControlLoop     : realisedBy

' Layout only. Each pair of leaves stays under its own superclass, and the two
' arrangements that carry an automation stay out of the path between Action and
' ActionPath, where three edges already meet.
OpenAction     -[hidden]right- ClosedAction
OpenActionPath -[hidden]right- ClosedActionPath
ControlChain   -[hidden]right- ControlLoop

@enduml
